course: dictionary
lesson: 8563
title: Scared: a feeling and a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Scared» means feeling fear, frightened or afraid. You can be scared of something, such as «scared of spiders», or you can be scared to do something, such as «too scared to climb the tree».
explain: «Scared» can also be the past form of the verb «scare». In «The noise scared the dog», the noise is the thing that made the dog afraid. Look at the words around it to tell which kind of «scared» you are reading.
explain: Being scared is normal, and it can warn you of danger. That uh-oh feeling tells you to be careful. If you feel scared, take a few deep breaths, and talk to a trusted adult. Scared people can still be brave: being brave means doing the scary thing anyway.
fact: «Scared» means frightened or afraid.
fact: «Scared of» means afraid of something, as in «scared of spiders».
fact: «Scared» is also the past form of the verb «scare», as in «The noise scared the dog».
fact: Being scared is normal, and it can warn you of danger.
fact: If someone makes you feel scared, get away and tell an adult you trust.
exercise: In «The noise scared the dog», what kind of word is scared? | An adjective describing the dog | *A verb, the past form of scare | A noun, a name for a thing | A question word
exercise: Lily says, «I'm scared of spiders.» What does scared of mean here? | Bored by | *Afraid of | Excited about | Angry with
exercise: «Before a vaccination you can tell the nurse you are scared, look away, breathe out slowly and hold a hand.» Which step can help you feel calmer? | Stop talking to everyone | Run out of the room | *Breathe out slowly | Shout at the nurse
test: «Being brave means doing the scary thing anyway, not feeling no fear.» What does this tell you? | *Brave people can feel scared and still do the thing | Brave people never feel scared | Being scared means you are not brave at all | Scared people should never try anything new
test: If someone makes you feel scared, what should you do? | Keep it secret forever | Wait and see if it stops | *Get away and tell a trusted adult | Make them feel scared back
exam: Ella was ___ of the dark, so she left the landing light on. | Happy | Hungry | *Scared | Curious
